   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi Craig,<div><br></div><div>You need to put RTools make utilities on the system path. You can do this manually using your Advanced Systems Settings or using R - instructions are found <a href=\"https://cran.r-project.org/bin/windows/Rtools/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://cran.r-project.org/bin/windows/Rtools/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792461864851000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1iGp0VBEOYREt0qhyu1QoZ\">here</a> under the heading <font face=\"tahoma, sans-serif\">Putting RTools on the Path</font><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\">.</font></div><div><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\"><br></font></div><div><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\">Cheers,</font></div><div><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\">Andrea</font></div></div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_attr\">On Thu, Oct 14, 2021 at 2:48 AM Craig Marsh &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">craig....@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:<br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
