     3,
     "<div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_attr\">On Fri, 15 Oct 2021 at 5:15 AM, Andrea Havron &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">andrea...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:<br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left-width:1px;border-left-style:solid;padding-left:1ex;border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204)\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Hi Craig,<div><br></div><div>You need to put RTools make utilities on the system path. You can do this manually using your Advanced Systems Settings or using R - instructions are found <a href=\"https://cran.r-project.org/bin/windows/Rtools/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://cran.r-project.org/bin/windows/Rtools/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792461864862000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1LLUQXWlUu5oI_5AYs4MKe\">here</a> under the heading <font face=\"tahoma, sans-serif\" style=\"font-family:tahoma,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">Putting RTools on the Path</font><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">.</font></div><div><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></font></div><div><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">Cheers,</font></div><div><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">Andrea</font></div></div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_attr\">On Thu, Oct 14, 2021 at 2:48 AM Craig Marsh &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">craig....@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:<br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left-width:1px;border-left-style:solid;padding-left:1ex;border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204)\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Hi all,</div><div><br></div><div>Recently I changed computer and freshly installed TMB, but am getting an ambiguous &#39;compilation failed&#39; error. I did some googling and most people get this when rtools isn&#39;t installed, however I have checked that Rtools is available. The weird thing is when I install some github repos with TMB compiled code, it compiles fine. So I am thinking it is a path issue or something. Any tips would be appreciated.</div><div><br></div><pre style=\"font-family:monospace;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">#If you install package from source you must have Rtools right?</pre><pre style=\"font-family:monospace;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">install<span style=\"font-family:monospace;color:rgb(128,128,48)\">.</span>packages<span style=\"font-family:monospace;color:rgb(128,128,48)\">(</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;color:rgb(128,0,0)\">&quot;</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;color:rgb(0,0,230)\">TMB</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;color:rgb(128,0,0)\">&quot;</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;color:rgb(128,128,48)\">,</span>type<span style=\"font-family:monospace;color:rgb(128,128,48)\">=</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;color:rgb(128,0,0)\">&quot;</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;color:rgb(0,0,230)\">source</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;color:rgb(128,0,0)\">&quot;</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;color:rgb(128,128,48)\">)</span></pre><pre style=\"font-family:monospace\">library<span style=\"font-family:monospace;color:rgb(128,128,48)\">(</span><font style=\"font-family:monospace;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">TMB</font><span style=\"font-family:monospace;color:rgb(128,128,48)\">)</span><font style=\"font-family:monospace;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nrunExample</font><span style=\"font-family:monospace;color:rgb(128,128,48)\">(</span><font style=\"font-family:monospace;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">all</font><span style=\"font-family:monospace;color:rgb(128,128,48)\">=</span><font style=\"font-family:monospace;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">TRUE</font><span style=\"font-family:monospace;color:rgb(128,128,48)\">) ## get the error her